#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adapt to changes in installing and depending on Qiskit v1.0"
msgstr ""
"Mag-angkop sa mga pagbabago sa pag-install at pag-depende sa Qiskit v1.0"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package"
msgstr "I-install ang bagong Qiskit v1.0 package"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package {#install-the-new-qiskit-v10-package}"
msgstr ""
"I-install ang bagong Qiskit v1.0 package {#install-the-new-"
"qiskit-v10-package}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit v1.0 uses a different packaging structure than previous Qiskit "
"versions and will likely cause problems in environments that use packages "
"that are not ready for Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang Qiskit v1.0 ng ibang istraktura ng packaging kumpara sa mga "
"nakaraang bersyon ng Qiskit, at malamang na magdulot ito ng mga problema sa "
"mga environment na gumagamit ng mga package na hindi pa handa para sa Qiskit"
" v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not try to upgrade an existing Python virtual environment to Qiskit v1.0 in-place.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Huwag subukang i-upgrade ang isang existing na Python virtual environment papunta sa Qiskit v1.0 nang in-place.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not make similar breaking packaging changes in the future. This is a one-time event, at the release of Qiskit v1.0, specifically so that our packaging story will be as easy as possible in the future.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi na kami gagawa ng katulad na breaking packaging changes sa hinaharap. Isang beses lang itong mangyayari, sa paglabas ng Qiskit v1.0, para maging mas madali ang aming packaging sa hinaharap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide is divided into the following sections.  You only need to review "
"the sections that are relevant to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang gabay na ito ay nahahati sa mga sumusunod na seksyon. Basahin mo lang "
"ang mga seksyong may kaugnayan sa iyo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Users should read the [For users](#for-users) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dapat basahin ng mga user ang seksyong [Para sa mga user](#for-users).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you develop or maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, read the [For "
"developers](#for-developers) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung nagde-develop o nagma-maintain ka ng isang package na naka-depende sa "
"Qiskit, basahin ang seksyong [Para sa mga developer](#for-developers).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you encounter problems installing or importing Qiskit v1.0, review the "
"[Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung may mga problema ka sa pag-install o pag-import ng Qiskit v1.0, tingnan"
" ang seksyong [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are interested in understanding the old package structure and why it "
"changed, review the [overview of the breaking package "
"changes](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung gusto mong maunawaan ang lumang istraktura ng package at kung bakit ito"
" nagbago, tingnan ang [pangkalahatang-ideya ng mga breaking package "
"changes](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For users {#for-users}"
msgstr "Para sa mga user {#for-users}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You must start a new virtual environment to install Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"It is very tricky and error-prone to upgrade an existing installation in-place to Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangan kang magsimula ng bagong virtual environment para ma-install ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Napakahirap at madaling magkamali kapag ini-upgrade mo ang isang existing na installation nang in-place papunta sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The examples in this section use the `venv` module that is part of the Python standard library.\n"
"If you use a different tool, such as `virtualenv` or `conda`, consult its documentation for help.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ginagamit ng mga halimbawa sa seksyong ito ang `venv` module na bahagi ng Python standard library.\n"
"Kung gumagamit ka ng ibang tool, tulad ng `virtualenv` o `conda`, tingnan ang dokumentasyon nito para sa tulong.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For Linux and macOS commands, a bash-like syntax is used.\n"
"PowerShell is used for Windows commands.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga command sa Linux at macOS, ginagamit ang bash-like syntax.\n"
"PowerShell ang ginagamit para sa mga command sa Windows.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create the new environment {#create-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng bagong environment {#create-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a new virtual environment in each project directory you're working "
"in, using your preferred version of Python 3.8 or later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng bagong virtual environment sa bawat project directory na ginagawa "
"mo, gamit ang iyong preferred na bersyon ng Python 3.8 o mas bago.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. Activate the environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. I-activate ang environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install packages as desired.\n"
"You should do this by using only one `pip install` command with all the dependencies on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-install ng mga package ayon sa gusto mo.\n"
"Gawin ito sa pamamagitan ng isang `pip install` command lang na may lahat ng dependencies sa loob nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   You can optionally include additional packages by including them as "
"arguments.  For example:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Maaari kang magdagdag ng mga karagdagang package bilang mga argumento. "
"Halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Qiskit v1.0 includes breaking changes, so several packages are marked as "
"not-yet-compatible with it.  Therefore, you might see errors from `pip` "
"until new versions of those packages are released. Old versions of packages "
"might also depend on the legacy `qiskit-terra` package.  Such packages might"
" not return errors when running this command, but might raise an error when "
"running `import qiskit`.  You should not install any packages that depend "
"directly on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang Qiskit v1.0 ay may mga breaking change, kaya ilang package ang "
"minarkahan na hindi pa compatible dito. Dahil dito, maaaring makakita ka ng "
"mga error mula sa `pip` hanggang hindi pa naglalabas ng mga bagong bersyon "
"ang mga package na iyon. Ang mga lumang bersyon ng mga package ay maaari "
"ring mag-depende sa legacy na `qiskit-terra` package. Ang ganitong mga "
"package ay maaaring hindi mag-return ng mga error kapag pinatakbo mo ang "
"command na ito, ngunit maaaring mag-raise ng error kapag pinatakbo ang "
"`import qiskit`. Huwag mag-install ng anumang package na direktang naka-"
"depende sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"   For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   Isang paraan para ipagbawal ng `pip` ang `qiskit-terra` mula sa mga indibidwal na `install` command ay ang paggamit ng [constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) na nag-aatas na ang `qiskit-terra` ay nakatakda sa isang imposibleng bersyon.\n"
"   Halimbawa, ang isang constraints file na may linyang `qiskit-terra>=1.0` ay nangangahulugang kung may dependency na susubukang mag-install ng `qiskit-terra`, walang nai-publish na bersyon ang magtutugma sa mga requirement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Nagbigay kami ng ganitong file sa isang GitHub Gist sa "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), na "
"magagamit mo nang ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kung ang isang package ay nangangailangan ng `qiskit-terra`, makikita mo ang [resolution failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   Do not install packages that are incompatible with Qiskit v1.0 on this virtual environment.  If you need to use such packages, install them in a separate virtual environment with Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   Huwag mag-install ng mga package na hindi compatible sa Qiskit v1.0 sa virtual environment na ito. Kung kailangan mong gamitin ang ganitong mga package, i-install ang mga ito sa isang hiwalay na virtual environment na may Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you have an existing environment, you can use "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) to query the requirements of "
"your installed packages to see if they require `qiskit<1`.  For any that "
"require `qiskit<1`, check for updates that make it compatible with Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kung mayroon kang existing na environment, maaari mong gamitin ang "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) para i-query ang mga "
"requirement ng iyong mga naka-install na package para malaman kung "
"nangangailangan sila ng `qiskit<1`. Para sa mga nangangailangan ng "
"`qiskit<1`, maghanap ng mga update na ginagawa itong compatible sa Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you encounter issues, consult the [troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) "
"section, or ask on [Qiskit Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). If you think "
"there is a bug, you can [create an issue against "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kung may mga problema ka, tingnan ang seksyong "
"[troubleshooting](#troubleshooting), o magtanong sa [Qiskit "
"Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). Kung sa tingin mo ay may bug, maaari "
"kang [lumikha ng issue laban sa "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are not planning to use the environment immediately, use the "
"`deactivate` command to leave it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung hindi mo pa planong gamitin ang environment ngayon, gamitin ang "
"`deactivate` command para lumabas dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use the new environment {#use-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang bagong environment {#use-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each time you start a new command line session, you must navigate to your "
"project directory and \"activate\" the environment by running the `activate`"
" command:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa tuwing magsisimula ka ng bagong command line session, kailangan mong "
"pumunta sa iyong project directory at \"i-activate\" ang environment sa "
"pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng `activate` command:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For developers {#for-developers}"
msgstr "Para sa mga developer {#for-developers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, use this information to "
"learn how to correctly express your compatibility and test against Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung nagma-maintain ka ng isang package na naka-depende sa Qiskit, gamitin "
"ang impormasyong ito para malaman kung paano tama na ipahayag ang iyong "
"compatibility at mag-test laban sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recommendations for requirements {#recommendations-for-requirements}"
msgstr ""
"Mga rekomendasyon para sa mga requirement {#recommendations-for-"
"requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend that your package requires `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (or other appropriate lower bound) if you are not certain whether the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"This is [the same recommendation being made for NumPy 2.0 compatibility](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"
msgstr ""
"Inirerekomenda namin na ang iyong package ay nangangailangan ng `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (o iba pang angkop na lower bound) kung hindi ka sigurado kung compatible ang package sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Ito ay [ang parehong rekomendasyon na ginagawa para sa NumPy 2.0 compatibility](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Qiskit v1.0 release candidate, version 1.0.0rc1, will be released on 1 February 2024.\n"
"You should test your package against this, and as soon as possible, release a new (compatible) version of your package with its upper requirement unpinned.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang Qiskit v1.0 release candidate, bersyon 1.0.0rc1, ay ilalabas sa ika-1 ng Pebrero 2024.\n"
"Dapat mong i-test ang iyong package laban dito, at sa lalong madaling panahon, maglabas ng bagong (compatible) na bersyon ng iyong package na may na-unpin na upper requirement nito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommendations for testing against Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-for-"
"testing-against-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Mga rekomendasyon para sa pag-test laban sa Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-"
"for-testing-against-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These recommendations apply to testing proactively against the Qiskit `main`"
" branch, and to testing against the v1.0.0rc1 (and later, if applicable) "
"release candidate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nalalapat ang mga rekomendasyong ito sa proactive na pag-test laban sa "
"Qiskit `main` branch, at sa pag-test laban sa v1.0.0rc1 (at kung naaangkop, "
"mga susunod pa) release candidate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We do not recommend initially branch-protecting on CI success against the Qiskit `main` branch because Qiskit changes could prevent you from merging PRs.\n"
"After the release of Qiskit release candidates, and after all of your package's dependencies support Qiskit v1.0, we *do* recommend branch-protecting on success against the latest release candidate, to ensure that the package remains compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi namin inirerekomenda ang branch-protecting sa CI success laban sa Qiskit `main` branch sa simula dahil ang mga pagbabago sa Qiskit ay maaaring pumigil sa iyo sa pag-merge ng mga PR.\n"
"Pagkatapos ng paglabas ng mga Qiskit release candidate, at pagkatapos ma-support ng lahat ng dependencies ng iyong package ang Qiskit v1.0, *inirerekomenda* namin ang branch-protecting sa tagumpay laban sa pinakabagong release candidate, para matiyak na nananatiling compatible ang package sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If neither your package, nor any of its transitive dependencies, has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1`, you should create a testing virtual environment as you normally would, in a single `pip install` command, and directly specify `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` or `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` as appropriate.\n"
"This is the most reliable way to ensure that you have a completely valid environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung wala sa iyong package, ni sa alinman sa mga transitive dependency nito, ang may requirement pin sa `qiskit<1`, dapat kang lumikha ng testing virtual environment tulad ng karaniwan mo, sa isang `pip install` command, at direktang itukoy ang `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` o `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` ayon sa naaangkop.\n"
"Ito ang pinaka-maaasahang paraan para matiyak na mayroon kang ganap na valid na environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the only component of your package's dependency graph that has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1` is your own package, you might want to have your CI suite first temporarily patch your requirements file to allow Qiskit v1.0, and then install the environment in a single step as before.\n"
"Alternatively, use the following rules for general-purpose environment upgrades, but switch to single-environment resolution as soon as feasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang tanging bahagi ng dependency graph ng iyong package na may requirement pin sa `qiskit<1` ay ang iyong sariling package, maaari mong piliing unang pansamantalang i-patch ng iyong CI suite ang iyong requirements file para payagan ang Qiskit v1.0, at pagkatapos ay i-install ang environment sa isang hakbang tulad ng dati.\n"
"Bilang alternatibo, gamitin ang mga sumusunod na panuntunan para sa mga pangkalahatang layunin na pag-upgrade ng environment, ngunit lumipat sa single-environment resolution sa lalong madaling panahon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If at least one of your transitive dependencies does not yet have a release version that allows Qiskit v1.0 support, you must make manual changes.\n"
"There are several strategies to try, in approximate order of preference (most preferable to least):\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung hindi pa naglalabas ng release version na nagpapahintulot ng Qiskit v1.0 support ang hindi bababa sa isa sa iyong mga transitive dependency, kailangan mong gumawa ng mga manu-manong pagbabago.\n"
"Narito ang ilang estratehiya na dapat subukan, sa tinatayang pagkakasunod ng kagustuhan (pinaka-gusto hanggang pinaka-hindi gusto):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the problematic dependency from its own `main` branch, if its "
"development version has relaxed the pin, so you can build the test "
"environment in a single step.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-install ang problemadong dependency mula sa sarili nitong `main` branch, "
"kung ang development version nito ay nag-relax na ng pin, para mabuo mo ang "
"test environment sa isang hakbang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exclude the use of that dependency from the test environment, if possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibukod ang paggamit ng dependency na iyon mula sa test environment, kung "
"posible.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a test environment in the same way you would normally, and then "
"manually override it to use Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng test environment sa parehong paraan ng karaniwan mo, at pagkatapos"
" ay manu-manong i-override ito para gamitin ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Manually upgrade an existing environment {#manually-upgrade-an-existing-"
"environment}"
msgstr ""
"Manu-manong i-upgrade ang isang existing na environment {#manually-upgrade-"
"an-existing-environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"This process deliberately creates an invalid environment.  Therefore, any test using it is less valid. Tests might appear to pass, but this does not guarantee that the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.  This could happen because the environment is not self-consistent and could contain files that do not exist in a valid environment, or the behavior of an overridden package might change with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Sadyang lumilikha ng invalid na environment ang prosesong ito. Kaya naman, ang anumang test na gumagamit nito ay hindi gaanong valid. Maaaring lumabas na pumasa ang mga test, ngunit hindi ito ginagarantiyahan na compatible ang package sa Qiskit v1.0. Maaaring mangyari ito dahil ang environment ay hindi self-consistent at maaaring naglalaman ng mga file na wala sa isang valid na environment, o ang behavior ng isang overridden na package ay maaaring magbago sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If one of your dependencies pins `qiskit<1` even on their development branch, it might not work in any way with Qiskit v1.0, and if your tests cannot run because of this, you might have to wait for them (or work with them) to become compatible.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kung ang isa sa iyong mga dependency ay nag-pi-pin ng `qiskit<1` kahit sa kanilang development branch, maaaring hindi ito gumagana sa anumang paraan sa Qiskit v1.0, at kung hindi mapapatakbo ang iyong mga test dahil dito, maaaring kailangan mong hintayin sila (o makipagtulungan sa kanila) para maging compatible.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade an environment in situ, follow these steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para i-upgrade ang isang environment nang in situ, sundin ang mga hakbang na"
" ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create an environment as usual, ensuring that there are no packages that "
"extend the `qiskit` or `qiskit.providers` namespace installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng environment tulad ng karaniwan, at tiyaking walang mga package na "
"nagpapalawak ng `qiskit` o `qiskit.providers` namespace ang naka-install.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Uninstall both `qiskit` and `qiskit-terra` to make sure that neither is "
"present:\n"
msgstr ""
"I-uninstall ang parehong `qiskit` at `qiskit-terra` para matiyak na wala ang"
" isa man sa kanila:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  At this point, the environment's `site-packages` should not contain a `qiskit` directory. You don't need to verify this on every CI run, but if you are debugging a script locally, follow these steps to verify:\n"
"  1. Run the following command from within the `python` of the virtual environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa puntong ito, ang `site-packages` ng environment ay hindi dapat naglalaman ng `qiskit` directory. Hindi mo kailangang i-verify ito sa bawat CI run, ngunit kung nagde-debug ka ng script nang lokal, sundin ang mga hakbang na ito para ma-verify:\n"
"  1. Patakbuhin ang sumusunod na command mula sa loob ng `python` ng virtual environment:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. Verify that those directories do not contain a `qiskit` directory. If they do, you likely have namespace-extending packages installed, and you should find these and remove the dependency.\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. I-verify na ang mga directory na iyon ay hindi naglalaman ng `qiskit` directory. Kung naglalaman ang mga ito, malamang na mayroon kang mga namespace-extending na package na naka-install, at dapat mong hanapin at alisin ang dependency.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the target version of Qiskit v1.0 with one of these commands:\n"
msgstr ""
"I-install ang target na bersyon ng Qiskit v1.0 gamit ang isa sa mga command "
"na ito:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "After the  desired release candidate has been published:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ma-publish ang gustong release candidate:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * For a `main`-branch dependency (or substitute whatever `git` revision identifier you prefer after the `@`).\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * Para sa isang `main`-branch dependency (o palitan ang anumang `git` revision identifier na gusto mo pagkatapos ng `@`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You now have an environment that Qiskit allows you to test in. If `import "
"qiskit` results in an `ImportError`, or if you are struggling to find your "
"dependencies, see the advice in the section about the  [invalid-environment "
"protections](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) in Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon ka na ngayong environment na pinapayagan ka ng Qiskit na mag-test. "
"Kung ang `import qiskit` ay nagresulta sa `ImportError`, o kung nahihirapan "
"kang hanapin ang iyong mga dependency, tingnan ang payo sa seksyon tungkol "
"sa [invalid-environment protections](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) sa Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample manual GitHub Actions workflows {#sample-manual-github-actions-"
"workflows}"
msgstr ""
"Mga sample na manu-manong GitHub Actions workflows {#sample-manual-github-"
"actions-workflows}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following workflows set up a scheduled job to run overnight.  This job "
"sets up a testing environment for Qiskit v1.0 and runs `pytest` (or whatever"
" test steps you need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sumusunod na workflow ay nag-se-set up ng scheduled job na tatakbo "
"overnight. Ang job na ito ay nag-se-set up ng testing environment para sa "
"Qiskit v1.0 at nagpapatakbo ng `pytest` (o anumang test steps na kailangan "
"mo).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For a package that has no transitive dependencies `qiskit<1`:\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang package na walang transitive dependency na `qiskit<1`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a package that has unavoidable transitive dependencies that pin "
"`qiskit<1`, build an invalid environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang package na may hindi maiiwasang transitive dependency na nag-"
"pi-pin ng `qiskit<1`, bumuo ng invalid na environment:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sample `tox` configuration {#sample-tox-configuration}"
msgstr "Sample na `tox` configuration {#sample-tox-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following are examples of `tox.ini` sections to build a testing "
"environment for Qiskit v1.0 and run `pytest` (or whatever test steps you "
"need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sumusunod ay mga halimbawa ng mga seksyon ng `tox.ini` para bumuo ng"
" testing environment para sa Qiskit v1.0 at magpatakbo ng `pytest` (o "
"anumang test steps na kailangan mo).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If nothing prevents Qiskit v1.0 from being installed in a valid "
"environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung walang pumipigil sa Qiskit v1.0 na ma-install sa isang valid na "
"environment:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your package or a transitive dependency has an unavoidable pin on `qiskit<1`, we recommend doing this testing using the manual environment construction as in the above section, because `tox` introduces several complexities by being more strict about environment isolation and installation order.\n"
"This is correct behavior by `tox` (we shouldn't construct an invalid environment), but because we already know we're building an invalid environment, these checks get in the way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang iyong package o isang transitive dependency ay may hindi maiiwasang pin sa `qiskit<1`, inirerekomenda namin ang paggawa ng testing na ito gamit ang manu-manong pagtatayo ng environment tulad ng sa seksyon sa itaas, dahil ang `tox` ay nagdudulot ng ilang komplikasyon sa pamamagitan ng pagiging mas mahigpit tungkol sa environment isolation at installation order.\n"
"Ito ay tamang behavior ng `tox` (hindi dapat tayong bumuo ng invalid na environment), ngunit dahil alam na natin na nagtatayo tayo ng invalid na environment, ang mga tsek na ito ay nagiging sagabal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Pag-aayos ng mga Problema {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The packaging changes around Qiskit v1.0 are tricky, and Python's standard tool `pip` is not rich enough in some ways for us to communicate the changes in the distribution structures to it, which unfortunately might cause issues for users.\n"
"We have tried to make Qiskit fail quickly and loudly if it detects an invalid environment, without false positives.\n"
"We understand that users might find it annoying to get the error message, but in our experience, it's much better to be aware of the problem right away than for things to appear to be working on the surface, only to fail in subtle ways in the future.\n"
msgstr ""
"Medyo kumplikado ang mga pagbabago sa packaging sa paligid ng Qiskit v1.0, at hindi sapat ang karaniwang tool na `pip` ng Python para maihatid namin sa kanya ang mga pagbabago sa mga istruktura ng distribusyon, na maaaring magdulot ng mga problema para sa mga gumagamit.\n"
"Sinubukan naming gawing mabilis at malinaw ang pagpalya ng Qiskit kapag natukoy nito ang isang hindi wastong environment, nang walang mga maling positibo.\n"
"Nauunawaan namin na maaaring mainip ang mga gumagamit sa pagkakita ng mensahe ng error, ngunit sa aming karanasan, mas mabuting malaman agad ang problema kaysa sa mukhang gumagana ang lahat sa ibabaw, tapos mabibigo lang ito sa maingat na paraan sa hinaharap.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section contains packaging errors that you might see, and describes how"
" to resolve them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naglalaman ang seksyong ito ng mga error sa packaging na maaaring makita mo,"
" at inilalarawan kung paano ito ayusin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of these problems are not unique to Qiskit, so the advice is likely "
"relevant, even if the problematic parts are not related to Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karamihan sa mga problemang ito ay hindi natatangi sa Qiskit, kaya malamang "
"na relevant pa rin ang payo, kahit ang mga may problemang bahagi ay hindi "
"nauugnay sa Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` says \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'qiskit'\" "
"{#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"
msgstr ""
"Sinasabi ng `import qiskit` na \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named "
"'qiskit'\" {#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Python cannot find your Qiskit installation.\n"
msgstr "Hindi mahanap ng Python ang iyong Qiskit installation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you definitely installed Qiskit, then you probably do not have the correct virtual environment activated.\n"
"See the [section on activating a virtual environment](#activating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung siguradong na-install mo na ang Qiskit, malamang na hindi ka naka-activate sa tamang virtual environment.\n"
"Tingnan ang [seksyon sa pag-activate ng virtual environment](#activating-a-venv) para sa mga tagubilin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using Jupyter and see this, ensure that Jupyter is installed into the same virtual environment as Qiskit.\n"
"Exit Jupyter, activate the Qiskit virtual environment on the command line, run `pip install jupyterlab` (or whichever notebook interface you use), then reopen Jupyter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung gumagamit ka ng Jupyter at nakikita ito, siguraduhing naka-install ang Jupyter sa parehong virtual environment ng Qiskit.\n"
"Isara ang Jupyter, i-activate ang Qiskit virtual environment sa command line, patakbuhin ang `pip install jupyterlab` (o anumang notebook interface ang ginagamit mo), tapos buksan muli ang Jupyter.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` succeeds, but trying to do anything returns "
"\"AttributeError: module 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" {#import-qiskit-"
"succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-qiskit-has-"
"no-attribute}"
msgstr ""
"Nagtagumpay ang `import qiskit`, pero nagbabalik ng \"AttributeError: module"
" 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" kapag gumagawa ng kahit ano {#import-"
"qiskit-succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-"
"qiskit-has-no-attribute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This likely means that your environment had an old version of Qiskit in it alongside a package that extended its namespace (such as old versions of Qiskit Aer, or the long-obsolete Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider), and then Qiskit was uninstalled.\n"
"The easiest thing to do is to start a new virtual environment, and only install recent, non-obsolete packages into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malamang na ibig sabihin nito ay mayroon kang lumang bersyon ng Qiskit sa iyong environment kasabay ng isang package na pinalawak ang namespace nito (tulad ng mga lumang bersyon ng Qiskit Aer, o ang matagal nang lipas-panahong Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider), tapos na-uninstall ang Qiskit.\n"
"Ang pinakamadaling gawin ay magsimula ng bagong virtual environment, at mag-install lamang ng mga bago, hindi-lipas-panahong package dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have just started a new virtual environment, or you're sure that legacy packages are not the problem, make sure that your current working directory (the directory your shell session was in when you launched Python / Jupyter) does not contain a folder called `qiskit`.\n"
"Python's default rules search the current working directory very early in the search path when trying to `import` a module, so a directory with a duplicate name can cause import problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung kakagawa mo lang ng bagong virtual environment, o sigurado kang hindi ang mga legacy package ang problema, siguraduhin na ang iyong kasalukuyang working directory (ang directory kung saan naroroon ang iyong shell session nang inilunsad mo ang Python / Jupyter) ay hindi naglalaman ng folder na may pangalang `qiskit`.\n"
"Ang mga default na panuntunan ng Python ay naghahanap sa kasalukuyang working directory nang maaga sa search path kapag sinusubukang `import` ang isang module, kaya ang isang directory na may parehong pangalan ay maaaring magdulot ng mga problema sa pag-import.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` refuses to install some packages together {#pip-refuses-to-install-"
"some-packages-together}"
msgstr ""
"Tumatanggi ang `pip` na mag-install ng ilang package nang magkasama {#pip-"
"refuses-to-install-some-packages-together}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After running a `pip install` command with many items on it, you might see "
"an error such as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos patakbuhin ang isang `pip install` na command na may maraming "
"item, maaaring makakita ka ng error tulad ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This describes a true resolution conflict; there is no valid way to install "
"all of these distributions at the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalarawan nito ang isang tunay na conflict sa resolution; walang wastong "
"paraan para i-install nang sabay-sabay ang lahat ng distribution na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of Qiskit v1.0, this is likely because one of the distributions you are trying to install contains a requirement like `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"This means that the developers of that distribution have marked it as not (yet) compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa konteksto ng Qiskit v1.0, malamang ito ay dahil isa sa mga distribution na sinusubukan mong i-install ay naglalaman ng requirement tulad ng `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"Ibig sabihin nito, minarkahan ng mga developer ng distribution na iyon na hindi pa ito compatible sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can (politely) ask those developers when they will release a new version of their package that is compatible with Qiskit v1.0, but first check that they have no open issue or pull request already asking for this wherever they accept comments.\n"
"Be mindful that this takes time; please give the developers a month or so to prepare new versions of their distributions!\n"
"Until then, you cannot install that distribution alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"To continue using that distribution, create a new virtual environment and use Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 (or whichever version it supports) alongside that other package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang (magalang na) magtanong sa mga developer na iyon kung kailan sila maglalabas ng bagong bersyon ng kanilang package na compatible sa Qiskit v1.0, ngunit suriin muna kung mayroon silang bukas na issue o pull request na humihiling nito saan man nila tinatanggap ang mga komento.\n"
"Tandaan na tumatagal ito; pakibigyan ng mga developer ng isang buwan o higit pa para maghanda ng mga bagong bersyon ng kanilang mga distribution!\n"
"Hanggang noon, hindi mo maaaring i-install ang distribution na iyon kasabay ng Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Para mapatuloy ang paggamit ng distribution na iyon, gumawa ng bagong virtual environment at gamitin ang Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46 (o anumang bersyon ang sinusuportahan nito) kasabay ng ibang package na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you get this error, **do not** try to build the environment by calling `pip install` several times.\n"
"Those commands will probably not fail, but you will have created an invalid environment.\n"
"You would likely then see some of the other error messages described in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Kung nakuha mo ang error na ito, **huwag** subukang buuin ang environment sa pamamagitan ng paulit-ulit na pagtawag sa `pip install`.\n"
"Malamang na hindi mabibigo ang mga command na iyon, ngunit magagawa mo ang isang hindi wastong environment.\n"
"Malamang na makikita mo pagkatapos ang ilan sa iba pang mga mensahe ng error na inilarawan sa seksyong ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also read [the documentation from the Python packaging authority "
"about conflict resolution](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ka ring basahin ang [dokumentasyon mula sa Python packaging authority"
" tungkol sa conflict "
"resolution](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` succeeds but prints errors after running `pip install` commands {#pip-"
"succeeds-but-prints-errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"
msgstr ""
"Nagtatagumpay ang `pip` ngunit nagpi-print ng mga error pagkatapos "
"patakbuhin ang mga `pip install` na command {#pip-succeeds-but-prints-"
"errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You might see an error in the output of `pip`, such as the following:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring makakita ka ng error sa output ng `pip`, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The top line usually appears verbatim (as of `pip` 23.3), but second line changes depending on the exact problem, and there may be several lines like it.\n"
"`pip` is likely to then indicate that it did whatever you wanted successfully, despite the error message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang linya ay karaniwang lumalabas nang verbatim (mula sa `pip` 23.3), ngunit nagbabago ang pangalawang linya depende sa eksaktong problema, at maaaring may ilang linya tulad nito.\n"
"Malamang na ipahiwatig ng `pip` na nagawa nito ang lahat ng gusto mo nang matagumpay, sa kabila ng mensahe ng error.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that the environment is in conflict and you cannot be sure that it will work correctly.\n"
"To solve the problem, examine the list of messages from `pip` and determine if you need all of the packages that have conflicting requirements.\n"
"Sometimes there will be true conflicts between dependencies; you might need multiple virtual environments to separate out dependencies that have incompatible requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibig sabihin nito ay may conflict ang environment at hindi mo masigurado na gagana ito nang tama.\n"
"Para malutas ang problema, suriin ang listahan ng mga mensahe mula sa `pip` at alamin kung kailangan mo ba ang lahat ng package na may conflicting requirements.\n"
"Minsan ay magkakaroon ng tunay na conflict sa pagitan ng mga dependency; maaaring kailanganin mo ng maraming virtual environment para paghiwalayin ang mga dependency na may hindi compatible na requirements.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The safest choice is to begin a new virtual environment (or more than one, "
"if there are true conflicts), then delete the one in conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinakaligtas na pagpipilian ay magsimula ng bagong virtual environment "
"(o higit sa isa, kung may mga tunay na conflict), tapos burahin ang may "
"conflict.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When setting up virtual environments, run only one `pip install` command that includes all the dependencies you need.\n"
"This is the most reliable way for `pip` to find a properly resolved environment with no conflicts.\n"
"If you keep having problems with conflicts after setting up environments, avoid running any further `pip install` or `pip uninstall` commands; `pip` does not guarantee to keep the environment coherent on subsequent commands.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-set up ng mga virtual environment, magpatakbo ng isang `pip install` na command lang na kinabibilangan ng lahat ng dependency na kailangan mo.\n"
"Ito ang pinaka-maaasahang paraan para mahanap ng `pip` ang isang maayos na na-resolve na environment na walang mga conflict.\n"
"Kung patuloy kang nagkakaroon ng mga problema sa conflict pagkatapos mag-set up ng mga environment, iwasan ang pagpapatakbo ng anumang karagdagang `pip install` o `pip uninstall` na command; hindi ginagarantiyahan ng `pip` na mapapanatiling magkakaugnay ang environment sa mga kasunod na command.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you are concerned about working with multiple virtual environments, rest assured that Python development and use often involve several virtual environments. It's common and good practice to create new ones to work on separate projects.\n"
"When you're done with a virtual environment, you can simply delete its directory; there is no reason to keep multiple environments permanently.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kung nag-aalala ka tungkol sa pagtatrabaho sa maraming virtual environment, huwag mag-alala — karaniwang ginagamit ng Python development ang ilang virtual environment. Ito ay normal at magandang gawi na gumawa ng mga bago para sa magkahiwalay na proyekto.\n"
"Kapag tapos ka na sa isang virtual environment, maaari mo na lang tanggalin ang directory nito; walang dahilan para panatilihing permanente ang maraming environment.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` raises `ImportError` {#import-qiskit-raises-importerror}"
msgstr ""
"Nagpapataas ng `ImportError` ang `import qiskit` {#import-qiskit-raises-"
"importerror}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When running `import qiskit`, you might see an error such as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag pinatakbo ang `import qiskit`, maaaring makakita ka ng error tulad "
"ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"
msgstr ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"You might have run a completely valid `pip install` command, following all the recommendations in this guide, and still see this error message.\n"
"This is not your fault, but the error message is still correct, and Qiskit cannot safely load.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Maaaring nakapagpatakbo ka ng ganap na wastong `pip install` na command, sinunod ang lahat ng rekomendasyon sa gabay na ito, at nakita pa rin ang mensahe ng error na ito.\n"
"Hindi ito kasalanan mo, ngunit tama pa rin ang mensahe ng error, at hindi maligtas na ma-load ang Qiskit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error means that Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that includes both Qiskit v1.0 and an earlier version.\n"
"This is characterized by the `qiskit-terra` distribution being installed alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"You can check what distributions are installed by running `pip list`, but you cannot fix this by simply uninstalling `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ibig sabihin ng error ay naka-install ang Qiskit sa isang hindi wastong environment na kinabibilangan ng parehong Qiskit v1.0 at isang mas lumang bersyon.\n"
"Ito ay nailalarawan ng pag-install ng `qiskit-terra` na distribution kasabay ng Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Maaari mong suriin kung anong mga distribution ang naka-install sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng `pip list`, ngunit hindi mo ito maayos sa simpleng pag-uninstall ng `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, `qiskit>=1.0` and `qiskit-terra` are conflicting distributions, and cannot both be installed together.\n"
"Even more unfortunately, *we cannot communicate this conflict to `pip`* because of limitations in its metadata system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasamaang palad, ang `qiskit>=1.0` at `qiskit-terra` ay conflicting distributions, at hindi maaaring i-install ang dalawa nang sabay-sabay.\n"
"Mas masamang-masama pa, *hindi namin maikomunika ang conflict na ito sa `pip`* dahil sa mga limitasyon sa metadata system nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This error most frequently arises in one of two situations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang error na ito ay madalas na nangyayari sa isa sa dalawang sitwasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You ran something like `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-else`, and "
"`something-else` has a requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagpatakbo ka ng isang bagay tulad ng `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-"
"else`, at ang `something-else` ay may requirement sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You tried to run `pip install -U qiskit` in an existing environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinubukan mong patakbuhin ang `pip install -U qiskit` sa isang kasalukuyang "
"environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In both of these cases, there is no guarantee that `pip` will return a "
"helpful message to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa parehong kaso, walang garantiya na magbabalik ng kapaki-pakinabang na "
"mensahe ang `pip` sa iyo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang paraan para hilingin sa `pip` na ipagbawal ang `qiskit-terra` mula sa mga indibidwal na `install` na command ay ang paggamit ng [constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) na nangangailangan na ang `qiskit-terra` ay nakatakda sa isang imposibleng bersyon.\n"
"Halimbawa, ang isang constraints file na naglalaman ng linya `qiskit-terra>=1.0` ay nangangahulugang kung ang isang dependency ay susubukang mag-install ng `qiskit-terra`, walang mga na-publish na bersyon ang tutugma sa mga requirements.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbigay kami ng ganitong file sa isang GitHub Gist sa "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), na "
"maaari mong gamitin tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution "
"failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang isang package ay nangangailangan ng `qiskit-terra`, makikita mo ang"
" [isang resolution failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-environment-"
"for-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng gumaganang environment para sa Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No matter how this happened, it is much easier to make a new virtual "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaano man ito nangyari, mas madali pa ring gumawa ng bagong virtual "
"environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we need to find out which packages are introducing a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Using the broken environment, install `pipdeptree` from PyPI. This is a tool for generating dependency graphs:\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, kailangan nating alamin kung aling mga package ang nagpapakilala ng dependency sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Gamit ang sirang environment, i-install ang `pipdeptree` mula sa PyPI. Ito ay isang tool para sa pagbuo ng mga dependency graph:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ask it which packages are introducing dependencies on `qiskit-terra` and "
"`qiskit` (these are two separate commands):\n"
msgstr ""
"Itanong ito kung aling mga package ang nagpapakilala ng mga dependency sa "
"`qiskit-terra` at `qiskit` (dalawang magkahiwalay na command ito):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outputs might look something like:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga output ay maaaring magmukhang ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above example, we have two distributions that have declared "
"themselves compatible with Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` and `qiskit-ibm-"
"provider`), and one that still has a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halimbawa sa itaas, mayroon kaming dalawang distribution na nagdeklara ng"
" kanilang compatibility sa Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` at `qiskit-ibm-"
"provider`), at isa na mayroon pa ring dependency sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"This example is a flat dependency structure.\n"
"You might see a much deeper tree than this.\n"
"The packages that are directly dependent on `qiskit-terra` (lowest indentation) are most likely to be the problematic ones, but one farther down the tree could be problematic if it depends on a specific old version of some other package that has already been updated.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Ang halimbawang ito ay isang patag na istruktura ng dependency.\n"
"Maaaring makakita ka ng mas malalim na tree kaysa dito.\n"
"Ang mga package na direktang umaasa sa `qiskit-terra` (pinakamababang indentation) ang malamang na mga may problema, ngunit ang isa na mas malalim sa tree ay maaaring maging problema kung ito ay umaasa sa isang partikular na lumang bersyon ng ilang ibang package na na-update na.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Seeing a dependency on `qiskit-terra` can mean one of a few things:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagkakita ng dependency sa `qiskit-terra` ay maaaring mangahulugan ng "
"isa sa ilang bagay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is an old package, and will not be updated to support Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dependent ay isang lumang package, at hindi ito ia-update para "
"suportahan ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, there is no chance of using the package with Qiskit v1.0, and you will need to continue using a previous version of Qiskit.\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the dependent being at its latest version (assuming the environment is new, and you didn't pin it lower) and having a direct requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa kasong ito, walang pagkakataon na gamitin ang package sa Qiskit v1.0, at kailangan mong patuloy na gumamit ng nakaraang bersyon ng Qiskit.\n"
"  Karaniwan itong nailalarawan ng dependent na nasa pinakabagong bersyon nito (ipinagpapalagay na bago ang environment, at hindi mo ito pinababa) at may direktang requirement sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is a package that is actively maintained, but does not yet "
"support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dependent ay isang package na aktibong pinapanatili, ngunit hindi pa "
"sinusuportahan ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, you will need to wait for the developers to release a compatible version - please be patient!\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the installed distribution *not* being at its latest version, even though your installation command did not specify a version.\n"
"  You can check the latest release version of the distribution by finding its page on https://pypi.org/.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sa kasong ito, kailangan mong hintayin ang mga developer na maglabas ng compatible na bersyon — maging matiyaga!\n"
"  Karaniwan itong nailalarawan ng naka-install na distribution na *hindi* nasa pinakabagong bersyon nito, kahit na ang iyong command sa pag-install ay hindi nagtukoy ng bersyon.\n"
"  Maaari mong suriin ang pinakabagong release na bersyon ng distribution sa pamamagitan ng paghanap ng pahina nito sa https://pypi.org/.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  `pip` likely searched old versions of the package until it found one "
"(possibly from months or years ago) that depended only on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Malamang na naghanap ang `pip` sa mga lumang bersyon ng package hanggang "
"makahanap ito ng isa (maaaring mula ilang buwan o taon na ang nakakaraan) na"
" umasa lamang sa `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is what has happened in the example above.  At the time this document"
" was created, `qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` was the latest release version.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ito ang nangyari sa halimbawa sa itaas. Sa oras na nilikha ang dokumentong"
" ito, ang `qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` ang pinakabagong release na bersyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you constructed this environment out of several `pip install` commands (such as if the environment is old and has been updated), first try to install all of your packages by using a single `pip install` command when you build a new environment.\n"
"If the problem persists, at least one of the packages you want likely does not support Qiskit v1.0 yet, and `pip` is finding an old version that it believes will work because it doesn't know about the `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra` conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung binuo mo ang environment na ito mula sa ilang `pip install` na command (tulad ng kung ang environment ay luma na at na-update), subukan munang i-install ang lahat ng iyong package sa pamamagitan ng isang `pip install` na command kapag gumawa ka ng bagong environment.\n"
"Kung nananatili ang problema, malamang na hindi pa sinusuportahan ng kahit isa sa mga package na gusto mo ang Qiskit v1.0, at naghahanap ang `pip` ng lumang bersyon na sa tingin niya ay gagana dahil hindi nito alam ang conflict ng `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead, use the `pipdeptree` commands to identify which dependencies do not yet support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Exclude any packages that do not yet support Qiskit v1.0 when constructing a Qiskit v1.0 environment, or continue to use a prior version of Qiskit.\n"
"See [Create the new environment](#creating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halip, gamitin ang mga `pipdeptree` na command para matukoy kung aling mga dependency ang hindi pa sinusuportahan ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Ibukod ang anumang package na hindi pa sinusuportahan ang Qiskit v1.0 kapag bumubuo ng Qiskit v1.0 na environment, o patuloy na gumamit ng mas lumang bersyon ng Qiskit.\n"
"Tingnan ang [Gumawa ng bagong environment](#creating-a-venv) para sa mga tagubilin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The example in this section was generated before Qiskit v1.0 was released.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang halimbawa sa seksyong ito ay nabuo bago pa inilabas ang Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The \"old\" distribution in question (`qiskit-dynamics`) was behaving correctly; it was not known to support Qiskit v1.0 yet, so it marked that in its requirements.\n"
"It's not possible to backdate requirements changes to previously released versions, and `pip` will search arbitrarily far back to locate something that works when building an environment.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang \"lumang\" distribution na pinag-usapan (`qiskit-dynamics`) ay kumilos nang tama; hindi pa ito alam na sinusuportahan ang Qiskit v1.0, kaya minarkahan nito iyon sa mga requirements nito.\n"
"Hindi posible na i-backdate ang mga pagbabago sa requirements sa mga dating na-release na bersyon, at maghahanap ang `pip` nang arbitraryong malayo pabalik para makahanap ng isang bagay na gagana kapag bumubuo ng environment.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng gumaganang environment para sa Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46 {#create-a-"
"working-environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have a broken environment after trying to install Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46, the most likely situation is that `pip` installed Qiskit v1.0 because it tried to pick the latest versions of packages, even though it was not required.\n"
"The easiest way to fix this is to create a new virtual environment, then run a single `pip install` command that has all the packages you need, plus an explicit `'qiskit<1'` entry.\n"
"If `pip` successfully resolves this dependency graph, you should have a working virtual environment.\n"
"If at least one distribution requires Qiskit v1.0 or greater, `pip` should give you an error message explaining this, which looks like the one in [the section on failed resolutions](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung mayroon kang sirang environment pagkatapos subukang i-install ang Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46, ang pinaka-malamang na sitwasyon ay nag-install ang `pip` ng Qiskit v1.0 dahil sinubukan nitong pumili ng pinakabagong mga bersyon ng mga package, kahit hindi ito kinakailangan.\n"
"Ang pinakamadaling paraan para ayusin ito ay gumawa ng bagong virtual environment, tapos magpatakbo ng isang `pip install` na command na kinabibilangan ng lahat ng package na kailangan mo, kasama ang isang tahasang `'qiskit<1'` na entry.\n"
"Kung matagumpay na na-resolve ng `pip` ang dependency graph na ito, dapat ay magkaroon ka ng gumaganang virtual environment.\n"
"Kung kahit isa sa mga distribution ay nangangailangan ng Qiskit v1.0 o mas mataas, dapat magbigay ang `pip` ng mensahe ng error na nagpapaliwanag nito, na magmumukhang katulad ng nasa [seksyon sa mga nabigang resolution](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also use the `pipdeptree` commands listed in [Create a working "
"environment for Qiskit 1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) from within the broken "
"environment to determine which distributions have an explicit requirement on"
" `qiskit>=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ka ring gumamit ng mga `pipdeptree` na command na nakalista sa "
"[Gumawa ng gumaganang environment para sa Qiskit v1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) "
"mula sa loob ng sirang environment para alamin kung aling mga distribution "
"ang may tahasang requirement sa `qiskit>=1`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I'm a developer, my environments are definitely right, and I'm still getting"
" the error {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-im-"
"still-getting-the-error}"
msgstr ""
"Developer ako, sigurado akong tama ang mga environment ko, at nakakakuha pa "
"rin ako ng error {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-"
"im-still-getting-the-error}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First: you must be *absolutely* certain that your environments are correct.\n"
"The test that Qiskit uses to determine a broken environment is quite robust; specifically, it queries `importlib.metadata` for distribution information on installed packages and checks the version numbers returned.\n"
"The Qiskit v1.0 side of the test also checks for sentinel files that were present in old Qiskit versions and not Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una: kailangan mong *ganap na* sigurado na tama ang iyong mga environment.\n"
"Ang test na ginagamit ng Qiskit para matukoy ang sirang environment ay medyo matibay; partikular, nagtatanong ito sa `importlib.metadata` para sa impormasyon ng distribution sa mga naka-install na package at sinusuri ang mga numero ng bersyon na ibinalik.\n"
"Sinusuri rin ng Qiskit v1.0 na bahagi ng test ang mga sentinel file na naroon sa mga lumang bersyon ng Qiskit ngunit wala sa Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are a Qiskit developer, it's possible that you have old `qiskit.egg-info` or `qiskit-terra.egg-info` (or `*.dist-info`) directories present on your meta path (see `sys.meta_path`), left over from old editable installations.\n"
"In particular, check your working directory for any `*.egg-info` and `*.dist-info` directories.\n"
"If they're in the root of one of your checked out repositories, you can delete them. The worst that can happen is you might need to `pip install -e .` again, and even that is unlikely, because these are typically just part of the `setuptools` build process that doesn't get cleaned up.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung isa kang Qiskit developer, posible na mayroon kang mga lumang `qiskit.egg-info` o `qiskit-terra.egg-info` (o `*.dist-info`) na directory na naroroon sa iyong meta path (tingnan ang `sys.meta_path`), naiwan mula sa mga lumang editable installation.\n"
"Sa partikular, suriin ang iyong working directory para sa anumang `*.egg-info` at `*.dist-info` na directory.\n"
"Kung nasa root ng isa sa iyong mga checked out na repository, maaari mo itong burahin. Ang pinakamasamang maaaring mangyari ay maaaring kailangan mong `pip install -e .` muli, at kahit iyon ay malamang na hindi, dahil ang mga ito ay karaniwang bahagi lamang ng `setuptools` na proseso ng build na hindi nalilinis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the above information does not help you and you are 100% sure that your "
"environment is sound (or you are deliberately trying to test a broken "
"environment):\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung hindi nakatulong ang impormasyong nasa itaas at 100% sigurado ka na "
"maayos ang iyong environment (o sadya mong sinusubukan ang isang sirang "
"environment):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Create an issue in "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose) explaining how "
"this happened and why you are sure the environment is correct so we can fix "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Gumawa ng issue sa "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose) na "
"nagpapaliwanag kung paano ito nangyari at kung bakit sigurado ka na tama ang"
" environment para maayos namin ito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can suppress the exception by setting the environment variable "
"`QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong pigilin ang exception sa pamamagitan ng pag-set ng environment "
"variable na `QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
